/* ── v1.21 D7: Remote Control privacy-critical consent body ── */
"advanced.remote_consent_body" = "When this is on, your other signed-in devices can send this account's Macs four kinds of request, and nothing else:
• set a fan target, or revert the fan to automatic
• turn Low Power Mode on or off
• turn Keep Awake on or off

The server rejects any other kind, allows at most 6 requests a minute, and only for devices on your own account.

What never leaves your device:
• provider API keys, cookies, OAuth tokens
• transcripts, session logs, terminal output
• full project paths

A request is only a request. The receiving Mac honours it only if \"Remote machine control\" is also on there, every fan hold reverts on its own, and nothing here can run a command or control a process.

This switch used to also enable remote CLI sessions and permission approvals. Those have been withdrawn.";

